## Documentation Organization

All documentation MUST follow this structure. Do NOT create markdown files in the project root.

### Documentation Structure
```
docs/
├── README.md                 # Documentation index (entry point)
├── api.md                    # API reference
├── development.md            # Development guide
├── docker.md                 # Docker guide
├── testing.md                # Testing overview
├── TECHNICAL_OVERVIEW.md     # Architecture overview
│
├── features/                 # Feature documentation (one per feature)
│   ├── data-dictionary.md
│   ├── ml-development.md
│   ├── files.md
│   ├── gdrive-integration.md
│   ├── data-lineage-complete.md
│   └── m5-dataset.md
│
├── setup/                    # Setup & installation guides
│   ├── INSTALLATION.md
│   ├── DATABASE_SETUP.md
│   ├── ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES.md
│   └── *.md
│
├── guides/                   # User guides & tutorials
│   ├── QUICKSTART.md
│   ├── START_HERE.md
│   └── *.md
│
├── plans/                    # Roadmaps, improvement plans, status
│   ├── CODEBASE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md   # Master improvement plan
│   ├── PARALLEL_EXECUTION_PLAN.md     # Parallel work streams
│   ├── FEATURE_ROADMAP.md             # Feature roadmap
│   ├── FEATURE_STATUS.md              # Current feature status
│   ├── PHASE_2_ROADMAP.md
│   └── */                             # Feature-specific plans
│
├── reference/                # Technical reference docs
│   ├── ML_API_QUICK_REFERENCE.md
│   ├── ML_MODEL_DEVELOPMENT.md
│   ├── MCP_DATA_DICTIONARY_DESIGN.md
│   ├── GPU_RUNNER_QUICKSTART.md
│   └── *.md
│
├── branding/                 # Style & branding guides
│   ├── BRANDING.md
│   └── COLOR_SCHEME.md
│
├── testing/                  # Test documentation & procedures
│   ├── TESTING_GUIDE.md
│   ├── RUN_TESTS.md
│   └── TEST_*.md
│
└── archive/                  # Historical docs (read-only)
    ├── bug-fixes/
    └── implementation-notes/
```

### Rules for Documentation
1. **NO markdown files in project root** - Only `README.md` belongs there
2. **Feature docs** → `docs/features/` - One consolidated doc per feature
3. **Setup guides** → `docs/setup/` - Installation and configuration
4. **User guides** → `docs/guides/` - How-to tutorials
5. **Plans & roadmaps** → `docs/plans/` - All planning documents
6. **Technical references** → `docs/reference/` - API refs, ML docs, MCP specs
7. **Branding/style** → `docs/branding/` - Visual guidelines
8. **Test docs** → `docs/testing/` - Test procedures and guides
9. **Historical notes** → `docs/archive/` - Bug fixes, implementation notes
10. **Scripts** → `scripts/` folder - All .bat, .sh, .ps1 files

### When Creating New Documentation
- For a **new feature**: Create `docs/features/<feature-name>.md`
- For **setup instructions**: Create in `docs/setup/`
- For **roadmaps/plans**: Create in `docs/plans/`
- For **technical references**: Create in `docs/reference/`
- For **implementation notes**: These are temporary; archive when done
- For **bug fix notes**: Archive to `docs/archive/bug-fixes/` when resolved

